* L57b: bav199_fit.lib con CJO raddoppiata (3,7 pF): la sensibilita' del costo alla capacita'
* bav199_fit.lib - ESTIMATE of one diode of the Nexperia BAV199, SOT23.
* THIS IS NOT THE MANUFACTURER'S MODEL. Nexperia's own SPICE model could
* not be downloaded (assets.nexperia.com and www.nexperia.com answer
* HTTP 403 to automated clients; L57b). Replace this file with the
* manufacturer's model when it is available.
*
* USAGE (one diode per .MODEL; the part is two diodes in series, so
* instantiate two):
*   .include models/diodes/bav199_fit.lib
*   D1 anode cathode BAV199
* Pinout of the real part (datasheet p. 1): pin 1 = A1, pin 2 = K2,
* pin 3 = K1/A2 (common node).
*
* HOW IT WAS BUILT
*  - STATIC part (IS RS IKF N ISR NR BV IBV EG, FC, TT): copied
*    unchanged from .MODEL D1N914 of models/diodes/1n4148.lib (onsemi,
*    frozen at vendor/diodes/onsemi/1N4148/1n914.lib).
*  - CAPACITANCE: CJO=1.85p VJ=0.7 M=0.25, fitted by eye to Fig. 5 of the
*    BAV199 datasheet (p. 4, typical, per diode, 1 MHz, 25 C), which was
*    READ BY EYE from the plot: about 1.85 pF at 0 V, 1.1 at 5 V,
*    0.9 at 10 V, 0.7 at 20 V. The datasheet table (p. 3) gives only
*    Cd typ 2 pF at 0 V.
*
* WHAT IS WRONG ON PURPOSE - read before using a number from it
*  - LEAKAGE is the 1N4148's (IS = 3.45 nA, ISR = 1.01 nA): an UPPER
*    bound, far above the BAV199 (typ 3 pA, max 5 nA at 75 V, 25 C,
*    datasheet p. 3; no figure at 5 V exists in the datasheet). Any
*    offset or leak computed with this model is a ceiling, not a
*    prediction; the real part is orders of magnitude better at 25 C.
*  - VF is the 1N4148's: datasheet BAV199 gives only maxima
*    (0.9 V at 1 mA, 1 V at 10 mA).
*  - TT is the D1N914's 10 ns, not the BAV199's trr (0.8 us typ).
*  - No flicker noise, no temperature behaviour beyond EG.
*
.MODEL BAV199 D
+ IS=3.45e-09
+ RS=0.452422
+ IKF=0.0528
+ N=1.94
+ ISR=1.01e-09
+ NR=2.0
+ CJO=3.7e-12
+ M=0.25
+ VJ=0.7
+ FC=0.5
+ TT=1.012e-8
+ BV=100
+ IBV=1e-05
+ EG=0.92
